// Adversarial: Tether-Cascade synergy at 3 stacks each. Tether redirects 45% of every
// damage event to the linked partner cell (non-lethal spread). When a linked partner
// accumulates enough redirected damage to die, Cascade fires on all of its alive
// neighbours, healing them -- including cells that are themselves in an active tether
// pair. This creates a feedback loop: Cascade heals a cell back above zero, Tether
// respreads the next bolt hit to its (now healthy) partner, Cascade heals again.
//
// Dense layout maximises the number of eligible adjacent pairs so Tether links ~60%
// of all pairs at stack 3, and the Cascade ring reaches multiple linked cells
// simultaneously. The adversarial risk: in the same tick that cell B dies from
// redirected Tether damage, Cascade heals cell A (the primary hit target) whose
// HP may have just reached 0 from a concurrent primary hit -- if Cascade heals a
// Dead-marked cell, NaN can propagate into the heal arithmetic. If multiple Cascade
// heals and Tether redirects land in the same tick, entity count grows transiently;
// NoEntityLeaks catches any Cascade ring-heal entity that fails to clean up.
// HazardStackValid confirms both Tether and Cascade entries stay ≥ 1 stack throughout.
//
// Chaos input 0.6 drives rapid bolt bumps to maximise the frequency of concurrent
// Tether-redirect + Cascade-heal events. 6000 frames with allow_early_end: false
// ensures the feedback loop runs long enough to expose timing bugs.
(
    breaker: "Aegis",
    layout: "Dense",
    input: Chaos((action_prob: 0.6)),
    max_frames: 6000,
    disallowed_failures: [BoltInBounds, BreakerCountReasonable, BreakerInBounds, HazardStackValid, NoEntityLeaks, NoNaN],
    allowed_failures: None,
    debug_setup: None,
    allow_early_end: false,
    seed: 5513,
    frame_mutations: [
        (frame: 5,  mutation: InjectHazardStack(kind_name: "Tether",  stacks: 3)),
        (frame: 10, mutation: InjectHazardStack(kind_name: "Cascade", stacks: 3)),
    ],
)
